{"version":"1","id":"gamefromscratch","handle":"gamefromscratch","name":"Gamefromscratch","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--EcPfFcSs--/f_auto/v1724391677/logos/gamefromscratch","description":null,"is_squad":false,"x":-8.4188,"y":-7.7881,"cluster_id":1,"posts_collected":472,"newest_post_at":"2026-05-07T15:09:58.000Z","oldest_post_at":"2024-06-06T17:54:46.000Z","features":{"hype_score":0.112288,"listicle_ratio":0.004237,"question_ratio":0.029661,"avg_read_time":9.226695,"summary_length_avg":519.611111,"title_length_avg":56.222458,"title_length_var":358.088224,"tag_entropy":2.953547,"tag_diversity":0.190678,"top_tag_share":0.432203,"avg_upvotes":4.57839,"median_upvotes":1.0,"avg_comments":0.290254,"comment_to_upvote_ratio":0.06383,"zero_engagement_share":0.396186,"viral_share":0.004237,"posts_per_week":5.308407,"non_article_ratio":1.0,"author_present_share":0.0,"recency_skew":0.142857},"view_coords":{"engagement_style":[4.1324,5.9853],"cadence_depth":[8.3235,5.6912],"hype_variety":[9.4853,-2.6765],"title_style":[3.1029,0.8529]},"top_tags":[["game-development",356],["unreal-engine",143],["godot",133],["unity",131],["3d",96],["open-source",86],["blender",55],["ai",28]],"sample_titles":{"representative":["Zed code editor launches on Windows with performance focus","Complete guide to code editors and IDEs for developers in 2025","Godot's Popularity Explosion!"],"outlier":["Unity 7"]},"recent_posts":[{"id":"jgExCtYio","title":"Godot Popularity in 2026 (vs Unreal, Unity and Game Maker)","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VmUiR4dW8zw","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/godot-popularity-in-2026-vs-unreal-unity-and-game-maker--jgexctyio","summary":"An analysis of Godot's growing popularity compared to Unity, Unreal Engine, and Game Maker, using data from Godot's own website and Steam DB. Key findings: Godot has 1.8M Android installs, 1.2M Steam installs, and downloads per release have grown from ~800K in 2023 to ~2.6M for version 4.5. Steam games made with Godot roughly doubled between 2023 and 2024, largely at Unity's expense following Unity's controversial runtime fee announcement. On Steam in 2026, Unity leads with ~206 new titles, Unreal has ~107, Godot ~60, and Game Maker is declining. Unreal dominates in AAA revenue, Unity still owns mobile, and Godot is gaining ground primarily from Unity and Game Maker's user bases.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/VmUiR4dW8zw/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":1,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-05-07T15:09:58.000Z"},{"id":"YwzNKyKzK","title":"Unity AI open beta hands-on review of agentic and generative features","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=GCjrlpLhP24","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/unity-ai---slop-factory-or-awesome-new-tool--ywznkykzk","summary":"Unity has launched its AI toolset in open beta, integrating agentic, chat, and generative capabilities into the Unity editor. The agentic mode lets developers issue natural language commands to modify scenes, apply code, and instantiate assets, with undo support and transparent reasoning steps. The generative side covers 3D mesh creation (via Tripo and Hana 3D), animation generation, voice synthesis (via ElevenLabs), and sound effects. Credits cost $20 per 2,000, with pro accounts receiving 2,000 monthly for free. The agentic assistant is praised as genuinely useful for scene manipulation and prototyping, while 3D mesh generation results are poor and generative assets raise unresolved copyright concerns. Bringing your own AI model requires at least a $10/month subscription. Overall reception from the community has been polarized, with skepticism about AI-generated game content quality.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/GCjrlpLhP24/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-05-06T15:39:00.000Z"},{"id":"qYzuOceEb","title":"Free game dev assets roundup for May 2026","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=FAApDnEI2mM","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/free-gamedev-assets---may-2026-roundup-3dgamedevelopment-unity3d-unrealengine-godot-qyzuoceeb","summary":"A roundup of free game development assets available in May 2026. Highlights include three free assets from Epic Games on the Fab Marketplace (a low-polygon factory environment, a lens flare VFX pack for Unreal Engine, and a steampunk creature), available free until May 19th. Also covered: Kenny's updated input prompts pack (now with Steam controller and Oculus Quest icons), UModeler X for Unity (now free, enabling modeling, painting, texturing, and rigging inside Unity without sign-up), and new download options on Super Splat.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/FAApDnEI2mM/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":1,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-05-05T14:18:38.000Z"},{"id":"hXG2DF1hj","title":"Free game dev assets roundup for May 2026","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=DJpp9Q2O2XY","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/free-gamedev-assets---may-2026-roundup---unreal-unity-godot-more--hxg2df1hj","summary":"A bimonthly roundup of free game development assets covering several notable releases. Kenny's input prompts pack received new icons for Steam Controller, Valve Index, and Meta Quest. UModeler X, a modeling and rigging tool for Unity, has gone fully free with no login required. SuperSplat added downloadable 3D Gaussian splat files in PLY and SOG formats. Epic Games is offering three free Fab assets until May 19th: a sprite-based lens flare VFX pack with 300+ textures, a modular low-poly factory town compatible with Unity and Unreal Engine, and an animated steampunk saber-tooth tiger character.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/DJpp9Q2O2XY/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-05-05T14:18:08.000Z"},{"id":"lYoPAqrmm","title":"Anthropic x Blender: The Fallout!","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_suBlGBTlpQ","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/anthropic-x-blender-the-fallout--lyopaqrmm","summary":null,"image":"https: